# Skeleton-first loading

When building or updating pages and components in this repo:

- **Page / section / data loading** → use `Skeleton`, `PageSkeleton`, or a feature skeleton that mirrors the real layout.
- New App Router routes with async data must include `loading.tsx` (or a Suspense fallback) that renders Skeleton UI — never a centered spinner or “Loading…” text alone.
- Client refetch (filters, search, pagination) → Skeleton the loading region (table body, cards), not a blank area.
- **Spinners are only for micro-actions** — e.g. `Button isLoading` on form submit.
- Prefer composing from `@/components/ui/skeleton` and `@/components/layout/page-skeleton`.
- Do not invent alternate full-page loaders (Lottie, overlays) unless product explicitly asks.
